{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the leaders.</b> It is found in the last chapter of Yoma that the leaders were clouds. When the manna descended for Israel, precious stones and pearls would descend with it, and thus it says ״והם הביאו אותו״ — this is the manna about which it is said ״בבקר בבקר״. And further, Rabbi Yochanan said: for two mornings they brought the entire donation of the Tabernacle, and had left over." "<b>The shoham stones, etc.</b> Each one a single stone, to inscribe his tribe upon it. And the shoham stones they all brought, and likewise the anointing oil."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:48.066730896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}